+     * Sorted descending
+     * All constant values
+     * Random values
+     * Extreme values (very large, very small, boundary values)
+   - Run your solution against these inputs using timeout
+   - Target: solution should finish in approximately 2 seconds or less (adjust based on problem time limit)
+   - Use the run_with_timeout tool to run tests: `python /tmp/perf_test.py` with timeout_seconds=10
+
+8. **Run the tests**:
+   - Use the bash tool to run `/tmp/stress_test.py` to verify correctness
+   - Use the run_with_timeout tool to run `/tmp/perf_test.py` with a 10-second timeout
+   - Both should pass without errors or timeouts
+
+If any test fails or performance is too slow, analyze the output, identify the issue, redesign the algorithm, and repeat phases 1-8. You have up to 5 iterations to get this right.
+
+Start now with Phase 1. Create the necessary files and run the tests. Report the results clearly.
+"""
